Question 5: ITT and TOT variation analysis\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\sl324\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In my simulation, the ITT estimate is about 0.007, while the TOT estimate is about 0.026. The ITT measures the effect of being assigned to treatment, regardless of whether units actually received it. Because compliance is imperfect (only a fraction of treated units receive the treatment, in this case., p == 0.7), the treatment effect is diluted in the ITT estimate. The TOT rescales the ITT by accounting for compliance and captures the effect among compliers only. As a result, the TOT is larger in magnitude than the ITT in this setting.}